			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845822">
									

<blockquote>
<p>The GOI then used this to its own advantage, killing targets and employees with high levels of skill/competence/important memories and then adding them to some central source (becoming a sort of librarian/bookkeeper of minds).</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Honestly not sure why you need to go here&#8230; its much more interesting of an anomaly without the edgy &quot;they used it to assassinate people&quot; trope.</em></p>
<hr />
<p>So the anomaly is interesting, but I feel your execution is fairly tropey. I'd be much more interested in a narrative about identity than about some mystical bad guy from a GOI.</p>
<p>Moreover, there's very little narrative here. As described it is a short concept that is focused on how the anomaly works, without more substantive storytelling.</p>
<p>I think this is a pretty novel idea, and could be used to tell an interesting story, so I would suggest workshopping some concepts that this anomaly could be used to explore.</p>

