<p>Thank you very much for your critique. It really means a lot. The Announcer is responsible for the horde, but not aware of the hordes existence or his part in making it. This story is about what happens when a version of him finally learns about the true nature of himself and his “siblings”. As for the connection between the man and beast, it’s symbolic of having a dream fulfilled that a person thought they wanted, but the reality was a lot different than what they’d expected. As for in-universe explanation, the creatures are the enforcers, making sure that the Virus spreads by blocking out every other sound.</p>
