			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845808">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: J SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Joke SCP, Comedy</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Standard SCP page</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: An incident involving a Scranton Reality Anchor releases a new element into the atmosphere: the Element of Surprise. This element affects the Hume levels on a small area around it, creating unforeseeable results akin to Alchemy (transformation of one element into another, creating life, etc).</p>
<p>Central Narrative: Following the incident researchers notice that their experiments are yielding crazy results. Both super advanced experiments and simple stuff like making grilled cheese present impossible outcomes. The page shows reports of some failed experiments and the comically truncated investigation to understand the phenomenon. Finally they isolate the new element and devise a way to contain it: a multilayered sphere made of random materials that can resist the alterations caused by the Element of Surprise, maintenance includes adding new layers at random intervals to prevent ruptures.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</p>
<ul>
<li>Cartoon-like humor with the failed experiments</li>
<li>New element that can be used in future articles and tales</li>
</ul>
<p>Additional Notes: I don't have a lot of expertise on Joke SCPs but this idea seemed worth investing on. I'm open to all crits and suggestions :)</p>

